{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1784881826,"nonce":"7R5BrMx/E/Xq5xUiCSleqmnHTz8=","target":"121a16bf1cac4f5e11c7625ab9f70f4e69e21197e914f80e9059eb793f5d8638","message":"**Parent:** ADR-0060 — Org settings surface (`docs/adr/0060-org-settings-connections-and-secret-management.md`).\n\n**What to build**\n\nThe **IaC / declarative** path for connections, with **single-owner precedence**. Add a `connections:` block to server config (Helm values → config), each entry `{ kind, base_url, credential: \u003cenv-var | secret-ref\u003e }` plus optional repos to bind. These are provisioned at boot, are **authoritative**, and are **read-only in the UI** (edit/delete disabled, labelled \"managed by configuration\"). This generalizes today's `SCARAB_GITHUB_APP_PEM[_FILE]` override from \"just the PEM\" to \"any connection + its credential.\"\n\nA connection is owned by exactly one source — config **or** DB, never both — to avoid config-vs-DB dual-write drift. Credential resolution is one path: **env-override → `SecretProvider`** (today's `connection_credential()` generalized).\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] A `connections:` config block is parsed and validated at boot; invalid/unresolvable credentials fail closed (per ADR-0048 startup discipline).\n- [ ] Config-declared connections are provisioned and usable (resolve credentials, own their bound repos) without any DB/UI action.\n- [ ] Config-owned connections render **read-only** in the Connections UI, labelled \"managed by configuration\"; edit/delete are disabled for them.\n- [ ] A connection cannot be defined in both config and DB; the ownership source is unambiguous and displayed.\n- [ ] Credential resolution honors env-override before the `SecretProvider` secret-ref, for both GitHub and Forgejo.\n- [ ] Test: a config-declared Forgejo connection boots, resolves its credential from an env-var, and is read-only via the API/UI.\n\n**Blocked by:** 8b3cf79 (Slice 4: Forgejo connection create — needs the connection store/model + credential-resolution path, and the Connections UI to mark read-only).","files":null}]}